From b5d62c3bf87eaf31f14913046263007087e619cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ljm-233 <2836583630@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:47:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] screencasting: drop the shmem buffer pool bound

It defended against a mechanism that does not exist. PipeWire negotiates
the buffer count for the stream and niri only allocates what it is asked
for via StreamFlags::ALLOC_BUFFERS, so the pool never grew past the
negotiated size. Measured across a 5.5 minute share at 60 Hz, the eviction
loop never fired once.

Upstream maintainer pointed this out in niri-wm/niri#4655: "The buffer
count is negotiated in PipeWire too, and niri has a limit of 16 buffers I
believe, so if it grows larger than that then it's a bug in PipeWire."

A note in the config module records why it is not there, so the next
person does not add it back.
---
 docs/wiki/Configuration:-Miscellaneous.md |  1 -
 niri-config/src/lib.rs                    |  1 -
 niri-config/src/screencasting.rs          | 31 +++++------------------
 src/screencasting/pw_utils.rs             | 24 ------------------
 4 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)

